From 878fdf86a1198d4c48588a5bcb556117dc0c0d4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhen XIN <lone.zen6@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 03:06:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] mips: ingenic: fix IRQ state across SMP startup and
 idle

MIPS brings secondary CPUs up with local interrupts disabled so that an
interrupt cannot arrive before per-CPU exception, timer, IRQ, RCU and
scheduler state is ready. The generic start_secondary() path explicitly
requires the platform smp_finish callback to enable interrupts before it
hands the CPU to cpu_startup_entry().

The Ingenic callback configured the mailbox and CP0 interrupt masks but
left the global interrupt-enable bit clear. CPU1 consequently reached its
first tick_nohz_idle_enter() with interrupts disabled, triggering the
lockdep assertion that the NO_HZ idle entry path must begin with IRQs
enabled.

The opposite ownership error existed in jz4780_smp_wait_irqoff(). Generic
idle code disables interrupts before invoking an irqoff architecture idle
callback and enables them after the callback returns. The Ingenic callback
enabled interrupts itself, so default_idle_call() observed an unexpected
IRQ state and RCU/lockdep boot tests warned in lockdep_hardirqs_off().

Restore the MIPS IRQ-state contracts at both boundaries: enable local
interrupts once, at the end of secondary CPU setup after mailbox, mask and
broadcast-timer initialization; and leave interrupts disabled when the
irqoff wait callback returns so the generic idle loop remains their sole
owner during each idle cycle.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/mips/ingenic/smp.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/ingenic/smp.c b/arch/mips/ingenic/smp.c
index e2e168c0ffd8..45f512c445dc 100644
--- a/arch/mips/ingenic/smp.c
+++ b/arch/mips/ingenic/smp.c
@@ -119,8 +119,6 @@ void jz4780_smp_wait_irqoff(void)
 		"	wait			\n"
 		"	.set pop		\n");
 	}
-
-	local_irq_enable();
 }
 
 void jz4780_smp_switch_irqcpu(int cpu)
@@ -475,6 +473,8 @@ static void ingenic_smp_finish(void)
 
 	/* force broadcast timer */
 	tick_broadcast_force();
+
+	local_irq_enable();
 }
 
 static void ingenic_xburst_send_ipi_single_locked(int cpu, unsigned int action)
